<title>USA: EMERGENCY WEATHER CONDITIONS - WSC - 04-FEB.</title>
<headline>EMERGENCY WEATHER CONDITIONS - WSC - 04-FEB.</headline>
<text>
<p>Tropical Cyclone Pancho-Helinda, with 60 mph winds, is in the southern Indian Ocean near 19s/86e, moving south at 6 mph. The storm will turn more to the southwest with time and weaken. This system will weaken rapidly during the next 24 hours. It will be a decreasing risk to shipping during this time.</p>
